# [FABLE-5] sq-hmd7l.29 — Geographica real-world micro SPATIAL-JOIN query
# "QUERY 19 - Intersects_GeoNames_LGD" (micro_joins.lst, geographica2.di.uoa.gr), pinned for
# scripts/bench/geo-same-box.sh (the GEO_GEOGRAPHICA=1 family; corpus recipe
# bench/geo/geographica.sh). TRANSLATIONS vs upstream (see bench/geo/README.md):
#   * GRAPH <http://geographica.di.uoa.gr/dataset/...> wrapper dropped — both
#     engines load the merged slice into the default graph; the per-dataset
#     predicate IRIs keep LGD/GeoNames distinguishable.
#   * COUNT-wrapped (counts-not-coordinates): only the result-set SIZE is
#     cross-checked between engines before any timing is trusted.
#   * the one LGD/GeoNames-only join in the suite: a ~21 990 x 12 097 cross
#   *   product under a geof: FILTER — NEITHER engine has an indexed spatial-join
#   *   path for it, so at the default per-workload cap this typically records
#   *   honest ERROR(timeout) rows on BOTH sides (that IS the comparative result).
# Oracle: COUNT must equal expected-geographica.tsv before timing is trusted.
PREFIX geof: <http://www.opengis.net/def/function/geosparql/>
SELECT (COUNT(*) AS ?n) WHERE {
  ?s1 <http://www.geonames.org/ontology#asWKT> ?o1 .
  ?s2 <http://linkedgeodata.org/ontology/asWKT> ?o2 .
  FILTER(geof:sfIntersects(?o1, ?o2))
}
